Oh no, I love 'em. I like to drop a few pickaxes on my main stash level
in the hope that some passing dwarf will pick it up and help clear the
level out. I also avoid killing rock moles, and will carry out
extensive excavations of my own.

I consider any tunnelled and lit space a good thing- the further I can
see, the less chance there is of getting snuck up on. A
totally-excavated and fully-lit stash level with an altar, some pools
and a half-dozen chests/iceboxes is my dream. A few boulders on the far
side so the RNG has some "out-of-sight" space to generate monsters, and
that would be about perfect. OK, so it means there are no corridors to
hide in on those rare occasions when dangerous monsters show up more
than 3 or 4 at a time, but I can keep a pre-engraved closet or boulder
fort or two for that purpose- after all, I'll see them coming in plenty
of time.

I've never actually achieved that ideal described above, but I usually
hollow out a good chunk of the middle of the level.
Firstly, I always make sure there are wide, well-lit, direct routes
between all useful features (namely stairs, trap doors, water sources &
altars), and at least 5 or 6 squares tunnelled out and lit in all
directions around each.

Once all the walls of my altar room are utterly destroyed, I'll
re-build them with wizard lock then open just one or two doors. Walls
made of doors are much better for controlling monster and pet movement-
You can decide on a whim where your entrances will be, and monsters
can't move in and out of them diagonally. Furthermore, if you need a
break, you can just zap the door closed again. The only disadvantage is
that you can't use the old "wall-bouncing magic-missile" trick to score
double hits on monsters, but that's a small price to pay imho.

I'll also often keep a long dead-end tunnel somewhere, often with a pit
or boulder at the end, into which I will throw all useless glass, flint
stones and so on. Finally, if the game is going well I'll usually keep
or tunnel out/wizlock a large room somewhere on the level to use as my
statue room. Everyone has to have a statue room. Don't you have one?


